From: Recalbox <recalbox@recalbox.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] video: gate NEON alpha blit on AArch64

Blit8888to8888PixelAlphaSwizzleNEON uses vqtbl1q_u8, vmlal_high_u8 and
vaddhn_high_u16, which are AArch64-only NEON intrinsics. The guard only
checks (__ARM_ARCH >= 8), which is also true on 32-bit ARMv8 targets
(e.g. Cortex-A53 built for arm-linux-gnueabihf, like rpi3/rpizero2),
where these intrinsics do not exist and the build fails. Require an
actual AArch64 target.

--- a/src/video/SDL_blit_A.c
+++ b/src/video/SDL_blit_A.c
@@ -743,5 +743,5 @@
 }

-#if defined(SDL_NEON_INTRINSICS) && (__ARM_ARCH >= 8)
+#if defined(SDL_NEON_INTRINSICS) && (__ARM_ARCH >= 8) && defined(__aarch64__)

 static void Blit8888to8888PixelAlphaSwizzleNEON(SDL_BlitInfo *info)
@@ -1005,5 +1005,5 @@
 #endif

-#if defined(SDL_NEON_INTRINSICS) && (__ARM_ARCH >= 8)
+#if defined(SDL_NEON_INTRINSICS) && (__ARM_ARCH >= 8) && defined(__aarch64__)
                 // To prevent "unused function" compiler warnings/errors
                 (void)Blit8888to8888PixelAlpha;
